NCT07882888.eligibility:
Inclusion Criteria:

* \- Aged 18-75 years, male or female;
* Histopathologically confirmed primary stage Ⅲ-Ⅳa surgically resectable oral squamous cell carcinoma, with measurable lesions (≥10 mm on spiral CT, meeting RECIST 1.1 criteria);
* ECOG performance status of 0 or 1;
* Expected survival ≥12 weeks;
* At least one measurable lesion per RECIST 1.1. Previously irradiated lesions may serve as measurable lesions provided disease progression has occurred;
* Availability of tumor tissue for PD-L1 testing (paraffin-embedded specimens obtained within 2 years or fresh tumor tissue);
* Adequate organ function assessed within 14 days prior to the first dose of study drug, defined as:
* Hematology: absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥1.5×10⁹/L, platelets (PLT) ≥100×10⁹/L, hemoglobin (HB) ≥9 g/dL (no blood transfusion or component transfusion within 14 days before testing);
* Hepatic: serum total bilirubin (TBIL) ≤1.5 × upper limit of normal (ULN); aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ≤2.5 × ULN (AST and ALT ≤5 × ULN permitted in the presence of liver metastases);
* Renal: serum creatinine \<1.5 × ULN, or creatinine clearance ≥60 mL/min; blood urea nitrogen ≤200 mg/L;
* Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) ≤1 × ULN. If TSH is abnormal, free triiodothyronine (FT3) and free thyroxine (FT4) shall be evaluated; subjects with normal FT3 and FT4 may be enrolled;
* Urine protein ≤1+. If urine protein \>1+, 24-hour urine protein quantification is required, with total urinary protein ≤1 g;
* Normal cardiac function: normal electrocardiogram (ECG) or ECG abnormalities of no clinical significance; left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) \>50% on echocardiography.
* Female subjects of reproductive potential must have a negative serum pregnancy test before the first dose of study drug;
* Male or female subjects of reproductive potential must use highly effective contraceptive methods throughout the study (e.g., oral contraceptives, intrauterine devices, abstinence, or barrier contraception combined with spermicide), and continue contraception for 90 days after treatment completion;
* Subjects voluntarily participate in the study, sign the informed consent form, demonstrate good compliance, and agree to follow-up.

Exclusion Criteria:

* \- Presence of distant metastatic lesions or locally unresectable disease (stage Ⅳb or Ⅳc);
* Prior primary nasopharyngeal carcinoma;
* Participation in another investigational drug/therapy clinical trial within 4 weeks before the first study drug dose;
